Z||000000||dennis_6||08-22-2001||08:23 PM||||My 86 Fiero SE v6 had a gas leak causing it to idle rough.  I know this because of the two foot flame that shot out around the distributor cap.  My guess is that the leaked seaped up around the rotor cap and when the rotor button made contact and sparked it ignited the fuel.  I just want to know if anyone has any ideals where it might be coming from and if I should even attempt to repair the fuel system or should I take it to shop.              Dennis||||reg||4
Z||000001||dennis_6||08-22-2001||09:26 PM||||If anyone knows what this could be could they please give me some help.  I did perform a search and got 46 results and not are really related.  My car makes a high pitch sound when it idles high kinda like a lose belt or a bad bearing.  I doubt it is either.   Thanks Dennis||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-22-2001||09:58 PM||||maybe you have ainjector leaking?as far as that noise thing depends where its ccoming from engine compartment/maybe a belt is loose  could be alternator getting ready to go south for the winter <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or if its coming from underneath it could be fuel pumpgetting ready to go you know where.to check where its leaking the gas that is.turn your key on let the pump charge the fuel system then look for leaks but I would not start the car let alone drive it till you get that leak fixed||||reg||1
Z||000003||dennis_6||08-22-2001||10:05 PM||||I really doubt it is the belts they are pretty new.  The altenator seems to be fine.  Fuel pump maybe.  I can't see the leak but I assume it is from a fuel rail or injectors.  Never had a problem with the injectors before.  Could the be a lose connection to the fuel rails?    ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-22-2001||10:16 PM||||Have you done any work on the engine recently?<BR>From the location given it may be possible, but I doubt it, that the #5 injector 'O' ring may be bad. Unless of course it happened on a COLD start, in which case the cold start injector is leaking somehow (that's my bet!).||||reg||1
Z||000005||dennis_6||08-22-2001||11:00 PM||||It might very well be the cold start injector I did just start the engine.  Could it be a recall problem.  I don't think this car has had any recall work done and 1800PMCARES tells me they won't do recall work on a car this old.  I have searched threads on this page telling me they can't say that.  If this is possible would someone let me know so maybe pontiac could pay the bill it is an Fiero engine fire.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||01:09 PM||||I think you need to call again when there are safety issues they have to fi the problem no matter how old ask to speak with someone else do not give up.||||reg||1
